iven by low housing inventory, elevated and volatile mortgage interest rates, changes in rental inventory and occupancy rates, as well as home price fluctuations and inflationary conditions. These factors may impact the number of transactions consumers complete using our products and services and demand for our advertising services. According to residential real estate data published by NAR, TTV increased 3% during the year ended December 31, 2025 as compared to the year ended December 31, 2024. We continue to invest in the growth of our business, which we believe has resulted in year over year total revenue results, described below, for the year ended December 31, 2025 as compared to the year ended December 31, 2024, that exceeded industry performance for the same period. The extent to which market factors impact our results and financial position will depend on future developments, which are uncertain and difficult to predict.","context":"Health of Housing Market","section":"Overview of our Business","block":610,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617640-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-11","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001617640","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1617640/000161764026000015/z-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/5e0b7c8427f6011b4590f60172b4b7ec8623dce8485d213eb6b8cf4ab75fe8a9.bin","sha256":"5e0b7c8427f6011b4590f60172b4b7ec8623dce8485d213eb6b8cf4ab75fe8a9"}},{"id":"b34e69eb97abfe4507a772dd9a5f05b8145e7df2d626fcb42b66b8114cf089cc","quote":"| | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | Outstanding Borrowingsat December 31, | | Lender | | Maturity Date | | Maximum Borrowing Capacity | | 2025 | | 2024 | | Weighted Average Interest Rateat December 31, 2025 JPMorgan Chase Bank, N.A. (1) | | April 28, 2026 | | $ | 200 | | | $ | 126 | | | $ | 72 | | | 5.41 | % Bank of Montreal (2) | | February 26, 2026 | |